          </mtable>
        </math>
      </maths>
    </div>
    <div id="p-0164" num="0196" class="description-paragraph">Explanation of symbols in Formula 4:
</div> <ul> <li id="ul0016-0001" num="0000"> <ul> <li id="ul0017-0001" num="0197">I(q): Absolute intensity-corrected SAXS profile (e<sup>2</sup>/nm<sup>3</sup>)</li> <li id="ul0017-0002" num="0198">Q: Scattering vector absolute value (nm<sup>−1</sup>)</li> <li id="ul0017-0003" num="0199">Δρ<sub>e</sub>: Electron density difference between air and membrane (e/nm<sup>3</sup>)</li> <li id="ul0017-0004" num="0200">S: Specific surface area (nm<sup>2</sup>) per 1 nm<sup>3 </sup> </li> </ul> </li> </ul>

    <div id="p-0165" num="0201" class="description-paragraph">
      <maths id="MATH-US-00010" num="00010">
        <math overflow="scroll">
          <mtable>
            <mtr>
              <mtd>
                <mrow>
                  <mi>d</mi>
                  <mo>=</mo>
                  <mrow>
                    <mn>3</mn>
                    <mo>⁢</mo>
                    <mrow>
                      <mi>P</mi>
                      <mo>/</mo>
                      <mn>5</mn>
                    </mrow>
                    <mo>⁢</mo>
                    <mn>0</mn>
                    <mo>⁢</mo>
                    <mi>S</mi>
                  </mrow>
                </mrow>
              </mtd>
              <mtd>
                <mrow>
                  <mtext>  </mtext>
                  <mrow>
                    <mi>Formula</mi>
                    <mo>⁢</mo>
